Package: medrev
Title: A Reproducible Toolkit for Biomedical Literature Reviews
Version: 0.7.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      given = "Imad",
      family = "El Badisy",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
      email = "elbadisyimad@gmail.com"
    )
  )
Description: An end-to-end workflow for topic-driven biomedical literature
    reviews. From a research question or a set of identifiers it searches the
    literature through the Europe PubMed Central REST service
    <https://europepmc.org/RestfulWebService>, which indexes all of 'PubMed'
    and 'MEDLINE', into a tidy record table with a stable schema. Records are
    de-duplicated, screening decisions are tracked with reasons, and every
    stage is logged so a 'PRISMA'-style flow of counts can be derived.
    Included open-access articles are resolved to a full-text PDF (Europe PMC
    full text, with optional 'Unpaywall' <https://unpaywall.org/> and
    publisher citation-metadata fallbacks) and downloaded with polite rate
    limiting and retries. Only open-access content is fetched; closed-access
    hits are reported, never scraped.
